格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Password-gated Cloudflare Tunnel access for the DeepSeek Harness Web GUI, with quick and named tunnel modes.","id":"gh:1334134217","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-auth-tunnel","slug":"ai-eks/dsh-auth-tunnel","topics":["cloudflare-tunnel","cloudflared","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","password-authentication","reverse-proxy","self-hosted","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Password-gated Cloudflare Tunnel access for the DeepSeek Harness Web GUI, with quick and named tunne"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"-gated Cloudflare Tunnel access for the DeepSeek Harness Web GUI, with quick and named tunnel modes."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Auth Tunnel"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Expose the DeepSeek Harness Web GUI through a password-protected Cloudflare Tunnel without changing "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"`deepseek-harness` itself."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- The `dsh` CLI and pnpm are available on `PATH`; the plugin command creates the Web profile when it"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" is missing.\n- `cloudflared` available on `PATH`, or an absolute `executable` configured for the plu"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"gin.\n- A long, random shared password stored as a DSH credential."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Install"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Install the latest published prerelease bundle from npm:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Or install the current sources from Git:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"This release targets DeepSeek Harness `0.2.0-rc.2` (the `0.2.0` prerelease), using its volatile Conf"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ig fields, configuration forms, and Plugins bundle page. Older Harness versions must pin a compatibl"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"e package version, immutable tag, or revision:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Git installs build the checked-out sources through `prepare`. pnpm 10 and later may first ask you to"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" allow that build in the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml`; follow the path and exact package key prin"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ted by `dsh` and then rerun the command."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"For a local checkout, build it before adding the path:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The bundle inserts and enables the `auth-tunnel` row in quick mode and replaces the Host-native dire"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ctory picker with the in-app browser picker. No `deepseek-harness` source edit or extra profile row "},{"id":"p18s3","text":" with the in-app browser picker. No `deepseek-harness` source edit or extra profile row is required."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Quick mode"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Quick mode is the default. Store the shared password in `$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml` (`$DSH_HOME` d"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"efaults to `~/.dsh`):"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Start the Web profile:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Starting before `DSH_WEB_PASSWORD` is configured no longer fails the Web profile. The plugin stays m"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ounted with an error status and starts the tunnel automatically after that credential is added."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"After the tunnel is ready, the terminal prints:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Open that URL and enter `DSH_WEB_PASSWORD` on the login page. Share the URL, not the password. The a"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ctive row also appears in Web Plugins."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Web settings"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"With the Loader `auth-tunnel` row enabled, open **Plugins → dsh-auth-tunnel** to edit every option. "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"Saving the **Enable public tunnel** switch immediately starts or stops the gate and `cloudflared` wh"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"ile keeping this card available. The card also shows applying, running, stopped, or failed state and"},{"id":"p29s4","text":" the current public URL."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"**Allow remote pages to change settings** is enabled by default. The shared access password is an ad"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ministrator credential: a signed-in public page can read and save the Auth Tunnel card and Language "},{"id":"p30s3","text":"preference without local setup. Disable this switch if authenticated public pages should not manage "},{"id":"p30s4","text":"the tunnel itself; enabling it again then requires a local page or the settings document. These writ"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"es use authenticated endpoints owned by this plugin. Configuration changes persist in the active pro"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"file’s `cordis.patch.yml`. The switch is a separate fence from the core Host configuration plane: th"},{"id":"p30s7","text":"e gate proxies `settings.*`, `credentials.*`, and `llm.*` straight to the Host for every authenticat"},{"id":"p30s8","text":"ed public page, except that core settings writes targeting the `auth-tunnel` namespace are rejected "},{"id":"p30s9","text":"and must use the fenced plugin endpoint. The bundle's immediate client entry publishes that authenti"},{"id":"p30s10","text":"cated route before configuration forms classify the browser. The public GUI therefore keeps full con"},{"id":"p30s11","text":"figuration parity with the local one — responses come back redacted, and a secret crosses the wire o"},{"id":"p30s12","text":"nly inside a write payload. Only one remote write is accepted at a time, and writes attempted while "},{"id":"p30s13","text":"ide a write payload. Only one remote write is accepted at a time, and writes attempted while  [长行截断]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"### Named tunnel mode"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"### Configuration reference"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Key | Type | Default | Effect |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- **Shared password, single-user administrator trust**: every password holder is treated as an admin"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"istrator and receives the whole Web GUI, including the Auth Tunnel card, its write-only password inp"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"ut, and Language preference by default. Disabling `allowRemoteSettings` removes those plugin-owned c"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"ontrols, but does not restrict the core Host configuration plane (settings, credentials, LLM catalog"},{"id":"p38s5","text":"), which is proxied to the Host for every authenticated public page. Responses are redacted and a se"},{"id":"p38s6","text":"cret travels only inside a write payload. There is no rate limiting, lockout, per-user session, or s"},{"id":"p38s7","text":"erver-side revocation list. Do not share this password with less-trusted viewers; stronger deploymen"},{"id":"p38s8","text":"ts should use Cloudflare Access or another identity-aware proxy. Password rotation invalidates every"},{"id":"p38s9","text":" session.\n- **Single tunnel, no automatic restart**: an unexpected `cloudflared` exit is logged and "},{"id":"p38s10","text":"shown in settings, but the tunnel does not restart automatically; toggle it off and on to recover.\n-"},{"id":"p38s11","text":" **Quick URLs change on every start**: use token mode and a domain when a stable URL is required.\n- "},{"id":"p38s12","text":"**Local DSH authentication remains enabled**: the shared password protects the tunnel path. Direct a"},{"id":"p38s13","text":"ccess to the original Web GUI uses the token-bearing URL printed by `dsh web` and DSH's browser sess"},{"id":"p38s14","text":"ion.\n- **Minimal child environment**: the child inherits only `PATH`, `HOME`, and `TMPDIR`. A corpor"},{"id":"p38s15","text":"ate proxy must be configured for `cloudflared` outside this plugin.\n- **Loopback HTTP is plaintext**"},{"id":"p38s16","text":": the gate and upstream WebServer communicate over same-host loopback HTTP; TLS terminates at Cloudf"},{"id":"p38s17","text":"lare.\n- **One directory-picker interaction per boot**: enabling the bundle uses the in-app browser p"},{"id":"p38s18","text":"icker for local clients too because the Web app cannot select native and browser pickers per connect"},{"id":"p38s19","text":"r for local clients too because the Web app cannot select native and browser pickers per connection."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
